# Supply-chain hardening (added 2026-08-18, Shai-Hulud / keyv-cacheable incident).
#
# Blocks preinstall/install/postinstall lifecycle scripts from dependencies.
# The Shai-Hulud worm family executes via a `preinstall` hook that runs
# `node setup.mjs`, harvesting npm/GitHub/AWS/K8s/Vault credentials and .env,
# SSH key and Terraform state files, then republishes itself using stolen tokens.
# With this flag those hooks never execute even if a poisoned version is fetched.
#
# KNOWN TRADE-OFF: some dependencies legitimately use postinstall to fetch a
# platform-specific binary. In this project that is `esbuild` (node install.js)
# and `unrs-resolver` (napi-postinstall). If a clean install ever fails to
# resolve a native binary, do NOT simply delete this line — instead allow only
# the specific package, e.g.:
#     npm rebuild esbuild
# after verifying the version is not a known-malicious one.
# nvm use && npm ci ignore-scripts && npm run dev
ignore-scripts=true
